//   wobble px), jitter 0.04 (luminance jitter of the colour), loop.
//   widths (ALL DOGS round 1, A3; lane KIT; brushStroke only): an array of FULL widths in user px (the unit of w) sampled along the path, read
//   by arc length through the shared PK.widthProfile (gesture.js; one per vertex when the array is the path's length, else spaced evenly over
//   the length, linear between; the old naraStroke's wAt).  The FOOTPRINT at every sample is the local width (hf is w(s) (FOOT0 + FOOT1 p)
//   in place of w (...)), the hairs (N from the profile's maximum) packing closer where it narrows; the DEPOSIT per hair per px is scaled by
//   w(s) / max, so the film's depth is the paint's wherever the stroke is and the paint per unit length follows the width (the load is spent
