//   that ends the stroke bare, or with a film under `close` x the stroke's own body film (the mean film of its fully covered cells), is a gap
//   the tuft's paint was squeezed over: it is brought to that film with the stroke's paint before the stroke's one deposit (AREA resolve), so it
//   goes down as the stroke's film at the stroke's alpha, thickness and wetness, no second gesture.  The soft fringe (hairs below CLOSE_C) is
//   outside the swath and stands; the HAIR COVER spread above the floor stands; only what would show the ground through a body pass is closed.
//   Absent or 0: the stroke as before, byte for byte (K.CLOSE 0 ignores a supplied close: the planted negative).  Control: harness/kit2_k5/.
//   brushFill adds: angle / ang / dir (deg:true), overlap 0.3 (alias spacing, gap), overProb 0.4 (alias overshoot), overLen (px), cover,
//   minLen 0.4 w, inset 0.5 w, fitWidth, shortAlt, contour (fraction of the perimeter re-brushed along the edge; contourEnds), color2 (graded
