    HAIR_LOAD: 0.4,  // the share of the tuft's load the least-favoured hair can spend before it stops (GROUP of it by hair group, the rest its own; see makeBristles): a hair stops when the tuft's mean x its share falls to REL_END, so the first hairs stop at mean REL_END / HAIR_LOAD and the last at REL_END; the dry end is hairs and groups of hairs still laying full colour beside hairs that have stopped.  0.4 (0.2 in round two): the tail of last hairs runs 2.5x the first, not 5x; a 5x tail is long, sparse and (its hairs alone under the tuft's mean pressure) pale: G20 0.064 at 0.2, 0.046 at 0.4, G12 along 30 -> 42
