    PICK: 0.035,     // fraction of the movable paint under a bristle taken into its load per new cell, at full contact
    DEP: 1.8,        // (round 7f, P7f step 2, header: THE FILM; round 8, P8 step 2: 1.5 to 1.8 with HAIR COVER.  Cover is concave in the film, 1 - e^(-2.2 film), so the same paint spread over full and thin streaks covers less than a flat film of it: P7f's 1.5 was the flat-film number for Nava's mean cover, 0.90 / 0.87 / 0.72 along the run; with his spread across (HAIR_COV) the tuft MEAN film is 1.8's, 1.06 in the middle, for the same mean cover, paint_film 0.928 / 0.860 / 0.736.  A flat film of 1.8 would cover 0.91 in the middle: the row that reads it is paint_hair_cover's SPREAD.)  paint released per bristle per device px at full contact, full load and zero speed: a full brush at press 0.7 and the arm's speed lays film 0.88 in the middle of its run (cover 0.86, COVER in layer.js), 1.3 where it lands (0.93) and 0.65 where it ends (0.75) at 1.5 with one value per hair; DRAIN scales with it so the hold in widths does not move: Nava's loads, read on N09, N04 and the tiger (Substrate_Integration6 step 1), land at 0.90, run at 0.87 and end at 0.72 over their grounds, and 6 to 21 percent of a window shows the ground under half cover between and through them.  Was 3.6 (film 2.2, cover 0.99 along the whole run, 0.96 at the end: the judge's "one even value", "extruded", "plastic"; two wet coats read as one, G10).  SPEND and the ridge's rate scale with it, so a load lasts the same widths; the enamel fill lays its own 6 (opaque by statement) and does not move.  Control paint_film (0.934 / 0.862 / 0.748 against 0.90 / 0.87 / 0.72 +-0.05; 1.3 reads 0.907 / 0.821 / 0.698, 1.7 0.953 / 0.893 / 0.790)
