// THE MODEL.  The pull is resampled at one device px; across it the footprint is 2 hw of one-px LANES, each lane a strip of the rag that walks
//   the pull carrying its own load (colour and amount).  At every sample and lane the cell under it is treated once per pull (a cell a bend
//   brings under two lanes is wiped once).
//   footprint   hard side: full weight to hw, off within one device px.  Torn side: the edge sits at hw x (1 - RAG x m(s)), m a two-scale 1-D
//               noise along the pull (cells 0.7 w and 0.15 w), so the edge wanders between 0.45 hw and hw; the weight falls over TORN_SOFT hw
//               (0.35: the rag's pressure lifts over a third of the half width) inside the edge, and the outer third of the torn side is eroded
//               by a soft 2-D noise (cells 0.2 w, HOLE 0.5 of the weight at most): the rag's lifted folds, not cuts.  With streaks 0 both
//               edges are hard (the W4 negative reads a ratio near 1).
//   streaks     st(u, s) in 0..1, the rag's folds across the width: two octaves of value noise, cells w/9 and w/28 across, 2.5 w and 1.2 w along,
//               mapped 0.25 + 1.3 n and clamped, so most of the width wipes near fully and a few narrow folds barely touch the paint (the thin
//               lines of the film left standing that make a wipe read as a wipe).  Toward the torn edge the cloth splays and the folds are pulled
//               to their mean (the fine octave by SPLAY 0.7, the coarse by half that, over the outer 0.15..0.85 of that half), so the torn boundary
//               is soft lane to lane, not only in its ramp.
