// ==== src/paint/ground.js
// paint/ground.js : the canvas under the paint, on the substrate (plan section 2.1 tooth row and the ground line of 2.4; lane P4).
// Two words act on PK.kit.paint directly, with no 2D-canvas drawing:
//
//   PK.paint.ground(L, rng, path, opts)   sets L.tooth inside path (null = the whole canvas) to the weave HEIGHT of cotton duck, and,
//                                          when opts.color is given, the base colour of the surface (flat colour, slow mottle, specks).
//       color    [r,g,b] | '#hex' | null    null (default) leaves col alone: the 2D ground already drawn was read by paintBegin
//       tooth    paint units               rms height of the weave (default L.opts.tooth, 0.045; one full loaded deposit is about 1.0)
//       cell     device px                 grain cell (default L.opts.toothCell, 1.7); the second octave and the thread pitch scale with it
//       weave    0..1                      thread tooth weight inside the height (0.5): warp and weft as anisotropic noise, pitch drifting,
//                                          each direction under its own 9 px mask so the two never sum to a grid (the M5 finding)
//       vary     0..1                      drift of the weave's weight across the canvas (0.8): the height scaled by a slow two-octave
//                                          mask (40 and 13 device px), 32 px tile rms CV about 0.2; the cloth is not even and the priming
//                                          fills it unevenly, so bare canvas reads in patches, not as one embossed texture (G19)
//     When paintBegin has already laid a whole-canvas field of the same tooth, cell, weave and vary, ground() keeps it (one pass, not two).
//       mottle   0..0.3                    slow uneven priming in the COLOUR (0.05 when color is given, else 0); warm 0..1 drifts it warm (0.5)
//       fibers   0..1                      dark specks 1-2 px, a dozen per 240x240 at 0.6 (0.6 when color is given, else 0)
//     Logs no mark: the material entry point (PK.ground) logs the 'ground' mark before routing here.  Draws rng.i(1e6) once for its seed.
//
//   PK.paint.toothField(L, seed, o, path)  the height model alone (o.tooth, o.cell, o.weave); paintBegin's tooth block calls it.
//
//   PK.paint.field(L, rng, poly, opts)    a house-paint field: the polygon is NEVER filled.  Wide lanes of a roller or a wide brush along
//                                          opts.angle, each a deposit run whose load falls slightly from where it started, lanes
//                                          overlapping by `overlap` of their width, edges soft and ragged, the odd dry-out where the roller
//                                          thinned; where a lane meets the polygon's edge the edge is displaced by a slow wander, so the
//                                          top of a field is a roller's edge and not a ruled line.  Deposits with L.depositAt only.
//       color    the paint                 angle rad (-0.12)   w  lane width, user px (min(canvas w,h)/9)   overlap fraction of w (0.15)
//       amount   deposit per cell (1.6: coverage 0.97)   thick (0.22: a lane is 0.35 high; two lanes 0.7)   wetness (0.35)
//       fall     load at the far end of a run relative to its start (0.12 = 12% less)   jitter per-lane colour (0.035)
//       dryout   0..1 how often and how far the load dips along a run (0.5)   ragged edge raggedness, fraction of w (0.06)
//       wander   lane centreline wander, fraction of w (0.015)   edge  rms px the field's edge strays from the polygon (7)
//       bead     extra height along each lane's edge, fraction of thick (0.35): the roller's edge bead, lit as a line at every seam
//       level    0..1 how far the film flows level before it sets (1).  House paint is self-levelling: the lap where two lanes overlap and
//                the roller's bead flow out over the lane spacing while the paint is open, and a set field on canvas is nearly flat, its
//                lanes left as COLOUR (lane tone, dry-out, the wandered edge), not as relief.  The laid height is levelled by a box mean of
//                width one lane spacing, twice (a triangle kernel: the seam train and its harmonics fall by 30x or more), over the field's
//                interior only; within 0.15 w of the field's edge the roller's soft edge and bead stand (the meniscus at a free edge), and
//                the volume is conserved to the cell sum (the paint went nowhere).  0 leaves the lanes as laid (a field still open, mid-roll).
//                Before this (P7b, Astra 5) N04's white and R02's sky rippled at 0.07 luminance peak to peak with a 100 px period, the lit
//                lap of every lane; on a set ground it is under 0.03 (rules/planted/paint_field_flat.js).
