//                runs warm (0.5)   mcell user px of the field's base octave at a 1000 px canvas (100; octaves at 2.6x and 6.5x)
//       drift    one gradient across the canvas's short side, half swing as a fraction of the value (0.03), direction from the seed.  mottle 0 drift 0 = the
//                coat before round 5, one colour per lane (paint_ground_mottle's planted negative: a 240 px window read 0.0020 to 0.0030 of its value in the slow band, Nava's bare canvas 0.0037 to 0.0070)
//       flat     (ALL DOGS round 2, K3; lane KIT) THE ROLLED FLAT PASS.  A large pale fill the painter laid flat (142's table, the story rooms'
//                tan fields) is neither the dry drags of a brush (the weave and the ground show in the lanes' dry-out) nor a glaze (a
//                transparent film that cannot lighten what is under it): it is house paint rolled out flat and even, one colour, its laps
