//                coat's mottle as the fill's slow field, no linear drift, a second coat (fieldK.LOADS_COAT2 of the bands, 1.0: a covering ground is two coats) brushed across the
//                first (fieldK.LOADS_CROSS) after the first has set, and the height the coats laid levelled as the roller's was (fieldK.LOADS_LEVEL: a ground coat is thin and flows level, so the loads are colour, not relief), the whole cured (dry) when wetness is 0.  The roller lanes above (level, bead, dryout, fall, drift,
//                the lane tone) are the ROLLER, kept for flat (the rolled flat pass is a roller by definition) and for loads: false or
//                fieldK.LOADS 0.  loadW: the band width in user px when the caller knows it (absent: the long side / LOADS_W).  Measured
//                (Ground_Round12_Receipt step 1): his grounds at 1024 px, W07 grey 1.3 to 2.5 loads per 100 px, two-deep 0.09 to 0.34,
