// ==== src/hand/ghost.js
// hand/ghost.js : the ghost word (lane K-WIPE, 2026-09-05).  A drawing that appears, is wiped away, and returns: Rita Ackermann's later
// pictures (a figure in dark line, chalky pink or white dragged across half of it so it half disappears, the line drawn again a little off).
// One word, so a scene says it once and the drop (drops/world) can report it.
//
//   h.ghost(drawFn, o) -> { pulls: [path, ...], shift: [dx, dy], drawn: bbox | null }
//     drawFn(h, opt)   draws the thing (a figure, a contour, an icon) with the hand's words.  Called twice: first with opt = { pass: 1, shift: [0, 0],
//                      P: identity, alpha: 1 }, then, after the wipes, with opt = { pass: 2, shift: [dx, dy], P: path | [paths] -> moved by shift,
//                      alpha: o.returnAlpha (0.8), light: true }, so the return is visibly a SECOND drawing: a little off, a little lighter.  A
//                      drawFn that ignores opt draws the return in place (the wipe still makes it a second drawing; the offset is the scene's job).
//     pulls 2          1..3 wipes across the drawing;  angle 0 (rad) the pulls' direction, each drawn within +-0.35 rad of it;  w U/6 (or wu in
//                      U): the rag's width;  strength 0.7;  tint (a colour on the rag, e.g. a chalky pink);  carry, pressure, tooth, under pass
//                      through to PK.wipe;  side: 'left' | 'right' | undefined (each pull draws its own)
//     shift U/40       the return's offset: a number (that far, in a direction drawn from the stream) or [dx, dy]
//     stages           ['draw', 'wipe', 'return'] (all): a scene or a control can stop after the wipe (the W8 measure reads the wiped first
//                      drawing alone) or skip the drawing
